    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d29">

                <pb facs="0122" n="26" xml:id="pg26"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.62119/64: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-06T18:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 6,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:48 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>539. Department’s telegram no. 404, August 26.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d29-f1"/>
                    Briand’s absence has delayed a reply. I gather that the French think that the
                    Allied Powers must be consulted and that identic action should be taken, and
                    that they have already so informed the Belgians. Article in newspaper here this
                    afternoon was inspired by leak from Belgian sources, but I understand that the
                    Foreign Office is publishing correction.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
